  "answer": "**Assumptions**\n- No material specified: showing every material in the model.\n- No atmosphere specified: assuming the ISS cabin preset.\n\n**Verdict**\n**PMMA is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 2 to 30 cm/s.\n**Nomex is not flammable at any modeled flow**: 21% O2 is below its minimum limiting O2 of 24.1%.\n**Cotton-fiberglass is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 1 to 40 cm/s.\n**Delrin is FLAMMABLE** at 21% O2 for modeled flows from 1 to 40 cm/s.\n\n**Key numbers**\n- Minimum limiting O2 for PMMA: 16.6% (90% band 15.8–17.4%) at 8 cm/s flow, 14.7 psia.\n- Minimum limiting O2 for Nomex: 24.1% (90% band 23.3–24.9%) at 8 cm/s flow, 14.7 psia.\n- Minimum limiting O2 for Cotton-fiberglass: 15.6% (90% band 14.8–16.4%) at 8 cm/s flow, 14.7 psia.\n- Minimum limiting O2 for Delrin: 15.1% (90% band 14.3–15.9%) at 8 cm/s flow, 14.7 psia.\n\n**Evidence**\n- MOCK-BASS-II-03 (BASS-II; PMMA, 21% O2, 14.7 psia, 10 cm/s) → burn\n- MOCK-SAFFIRE-04 (Saffire; PMMA, 21% O2, 14.7 psia, 20 cm/s) → burn\n- MOCK-BASS-II-07 (BASS-II; PMMA, 17% O2, 14.7 psia, 5 cm/s) → extinguish\n\n**Operational recommendation**\n- Treat the material as flammable in this atmosphere: minimize exposed quantity and keep it away from ignition sources.\n\n**Limits**\n- Numbers come from a placeholder mock model (synthetic, not NASA data) until the Layer 1 API is connected.\n- Decision support only, not a replacement for NASA-STD-6001 material testing.",
